On Tuesday, August 29, 2023 at 12:03:39=E2=80=AFPM UTC+2 marcb...@gmail.com=
 wrote:

I still do not understand the difference between bridi and jufra;=20
if I understand that bridi relates to propositions and jufra to sentences;=
=20
I understand that a proposition is always a sentence but a sentence is not=
=20
always a proposition; since interrogative, exhortative, desiderative and=20
exclamative utterances cannot be propositions, since they cannto be=20
affirmated or negated.=20

Am I right? Am I wrong?

So, were I right, the exercise: "Don't panic" should be only a jufra and=20
not a jufra and a bridi.


First, the word {jufra} is not used a lot in the reference grammar.

https://la-lojban.github.io/uncll/romoi/xhtml_no_chunks/

Some of the examples from there:

zoi .kuot. Socrates is mortal .kuot. cu glico jufra
The-text =E2=80=9C Socrates is mortal =E2=80=9D   is-an-English sentence.

Thus {jufra} refers to the text, to the surface form of the language.
As for {bridi} is refers to the relation e.g.
"x1 panics because of x2" can be a possible relation in English.

"Don't panic" is a text.
That you panic is a relation.
To this bridi-relation you apply illocution power (a command) getting=20
"Don't panic!".

There is also {brisni}, which roughly corresponds to what is called=20
"sentence" in the formal grammar in chapter 21:
https://la-lojban.github.io/uncll/romoi/xhtml_section_chunks/chapter-gramma=
rs.html
{ko na xalni} is a sentence, a brisni.
brisni is a again a text, a surface form of the language,

What's the difference between brisni and jufra?
jufra =3D x1 (text) is a sentence/statement about  x2=20
[topic/subject/predicate/focus] in language x3.

As you can see from the example above  "jufra" can be even a=20
statement/sentence not in Lojban. jufra can be very complex like "I know;=
=20
but he knew it was a lie."
As of {brisni} is refers to a rule of the formal Lojban grammar (but might=
=20
be boardly extended to some other languages).

When learning Lojban it's better to settle on the concept of bridi, brisni=
=20
and other formal rules. The concept of jufra is of less importance in=20
Lojban per se.=20

